    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0331" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12522: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Earle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-26T17:00:00+02:00">June 26, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 27—3:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>292. In a long conversation with the Foreign Minister he stated to me again and
                    again the strong desire of the King and Government to maintain cordial relations
                    with our country no matter what happens.</p>
                <p>He impressed me with his sincerity but this in no way changes my opinion that
                    Bulgaria will do exactly what Germany orders.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
